{"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to PostHog","anchor":"Sending-to-PostHog","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSetupError"]},{"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"]},{"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":") for your PostHog project in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the project token and the host, posts to the host’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/batch\/"},{"text":" with a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"splits each batch to PostHog’s limits (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":"). A batch with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The project token goes in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" leaves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an anonymous event. Its "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions enricher, also sent as "},{"code":"$session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record with no session is sent under its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record identifier. Its "},{"code":"uuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event carries "},{"code":"$process_person_profile: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"$geoip_disable: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The record’s vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier and trace context aren’t sent, and the standard context is sent as PostHog’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties ("},{"code":"$app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the like)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals, and a property whose name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":" or is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out and logged. A record the encoder can’t write is left out and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ISO 8601 form (NaN, infinite, or more than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int64.max"},{"type":"text","text":" milliseconds from 1970), and one too large"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for PostHog’s event limit. The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reason is a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to TraffluentCollector, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/us.i.posthog.com, https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com or your own","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: postHog)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what PostHog receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"PostHogEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"PostHogEncoding","modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/posthogencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogEncodingError":{"abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s requests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no record of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PostHogEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PostHogEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogencodingerror","title":"PostHogEncodingError"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the PostHog project of "},{"code":"projectToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at "},{"code":"host","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"URLSession.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of "},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"postHog","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"projectToken","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"host","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","text":"URL","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"